Home-directory files for the production machine. README and
sync_to_latest.sh are versioned in the repo under production_root/;
copy them to ~ after updating. secrets/ lives only on this machine.

How to start the service:

1. copy the settings from the secret manager into secrets/
  1.1. secrets/local_settings.py
  1.2. secrets/env
  then place them into the repo:
  1.3. cp secrets/local_settings.py mediacms/deploy/docker/local_settings.py
  1.4. cp secrets/env mediacms/.env
  (sync_to_latest.sh does steps 1.3-1.4 automatically on every update)

2. (first time) setup SAML configs
  2.1 Add identity provider settings (example in secret manager)
  2.2 run `bash fix_socialapp_settings.sh` to actually place the config into socialapp.settings
    - fail running this script will face the missing 'idp' error when accessing https://tube.corp.foundi.info/accounts/saml/foundi-info/metadata

3. start the service
  3.1 `bash start.sh`

How to update to the latest fd branch:

Phase 1 - local dev machine (sync fd against upstream):
  1. pull upstream into main:
     git fetch upstream
     git checkout main
     git merge --ff-only upstream/main
     git push origin main
     (one-time setup: git remote add upstream https://github.com/mediacms-io/mediacms.git)
  2. rebase fd onto the new main:
     git checkout fd
     git rebase main
     - resolve conflicts if they appear, then: git add <file> && git rebase --continue
  3. push: git push --force-with-lease origin fd

Phase 2 - production (this machine):
  1. run `bash sync_to_latest.sh`
     - hard-resets mediacms/ to origin/fd (manual edits to tracked files are discarded;
       .env and local_settings.py are untracked and restored from secrets/)
     - recreates the containers; migrations and collectstatic run automatically
       in the migrations service before web starts
  2. verify:
     cd mediacms
     docker compose ps
     docker compose logs --tail=100 web
